# Color Auto Detailing - Local Development

## Environment Setup

Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in your values:

```
# Supabase (database — leads, chat, etc.)
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT_ID.supabase.co
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# API Configuration
PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3001/api
API_URL=http://localhost:3001/api

# Contact form email (Resend)
RESEND_API_KEY=
CONTACT_TO_EMAIL=admin@colorautodetailing.com
CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL=no-reply@colorautodetailing.com

# OrbisX CRM (server-side — sync leads from contact form & dashboard)
ORBISX_API_KEY=
ORBISX_BUSINESS_ID=

# Google Analytics 4 (Public - visible in browser)
PUBLIC_GA_ID=G-XXXXXXXXXX

# Google Tag Manager (Public - visible in browser)
PUBLIC_GTM_ID=GTM-PMBBJ2B6

# Google Site Verification (Public - visible in browser)
PUBLIC_GOOGLE_SITE_VERIFICATION=

# reCAPTCHA v3 (https://www.google.com/recaptcha/admin)
# Get keys from: https://www.google.com/recaptcha/admin
PUBLIC_RECAPTCHA_SITE_KEY=
RECAPTCHA_SECRET_KEY=

# OpenAI Lead Qualification & AI Chat (Server-side)
OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
AI_QUALIFICATION_ENABLED=false
AI_CHAT_ENABLED=false
AI_EMPLOYEE_NAME=ColorAuto AI
PUBLIC_AI_CHAT_ENABLED=false
AI_REPLY_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD=0.4
AI_REPLY_RATE_LIMIT_MS=2000
SKIP_SMS_FOR_TEST_SESSIONS=true
CHAT_SMS_BRIDGE_ENABLED=true

# Quo / OpenPhone SMS (website chat → your phone)
QUO_API_KEY=
QUO_PHONE_NUMBER_ID=PNR55fJAMJ
# Send-from line (ID above, or E.164). Do NOT use the same number as QUO_SMS_NOTIFY_NUMBER.
# QUO_PHONE_NUMBER=+19706281505
# Personal cell for SMS alerts — must differ from your OpenPhone business line
QUO_SMS_NOTIFY_NUMBER=+1YOUR_PERSONAL_CELL
QUO_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# GA4 Reporting API (Server-side, for employee analytics dashboard)
# Create a service account in Google Cloud Console with GA4 read access
GA_PROPERTY_ID=
GA_CLIENT_EMAIL=
GA_PRIVATE_KEY=

# Database (if using a backend)
# DATABASE_URL=

# Authentication
# JWT_SECRET=
```

## Notes

- `PUBLIC_*` variables are exposed to the browser
- Other variables are server-side only
- Never commit `.env.local` with real credentials
